<title>POLAND: Poland cuts 10-year floating bond minimum price.</title>
<headline>Poland cuts 10-year floating bond minimum price.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland cut the minimum price of its floating 10-year bond to 99.57 from 99.60 at the last 10-year bond auction on September 10, the finance ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The average price fell to 99.66 from 99.73.</p>
<p>The treasury sold 210 million zlotys of the bonds after investors bid for 245 million zlotys.</p>
<p>The next 10-year bond tender will be December 10, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
